                <pb facs="0629" n="509" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg509"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.105/388: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >McGurk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-11T12:00:00-05:00">August 11,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>99. Legation’s 77, July 10, noon. The President signed Aarons’ commission and
                    delivered it to the Commandant of the Garde today.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McGurk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
